{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>My people</b> — He recalled the kindness that HaShem did for Israel on account of Balaam's counsel, when he counseled to destroy everything." "And the meaning of <b>what he answered him</b> — that I did not leave Balaam to curse you, and I commanded him, and he prophesied, for I placed My spirit upon him for your honor. And it is written, <b>and all that he answered him</b>, that he blessed you. And Joshua said: <b>by the word of Balaam</b>, and I delivered you from his hand." "And the meaning of <b>from Shittim</b> — for between Shittim, where Israel sinned there, and the Gilgal, there was only a short distance and the crossing of the Jordan. And he mentioned the Gilgal — for it is the beginning of the land of Israel. And so the meaning is: when you were close to entering the land, then you sinned a great sin, and you were all sons of death, and I spared you, and you entered the land, and I helped you. And all this I did, so that perhaps you will recognize the good I did for you, and this is <b>that you may know the righteous deeds of YHWH</b>."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:07.067586847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}